From: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] roamd: no self-update check on Beam WRT

On Beam WRT roamd is built in the firmware feed for aarch64_cortex-a73 and
updated with the other packages. The upstream feed has no build for that
CPU type, so the check would only ever report an unreachable index.
---
diff --git a/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c b/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c
index 538a778..97c18ae 100644
--- a/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c
+++ b/package/roamd/src/mesh_update.c
@@ -257,6 +257,16 @@ void mesh_self_check(void)
 	if (!job)
 		return;
 
+	/* On Beam WRT roamd comes from the firmware's own signed feed, built for
+	 * its CPU type, and is updated with the other packages. The upstream feed
+	 * has no build for it, so report the installed version as current. */
+	if (!access("/etc/be7000-release", F_OK)) {
+		selfcheck_write(job, true);
+		free(job);
+
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (!mesh_self_release(job->branch, sizeof(job->branch), job->arch, sizeof(job->arch))) {
 		selfcheck_write(job, false);
 		free(job);
